The program doing the analysis needs a lot of information.
Ideally, everything that comes out of the RGN, but at the very
least, the results of most, if not all, of the decisions based
on the RGN.

This is really the reason why I doubt such a bot is possible.
You don't see the output of the RNG in any way; you don't even
see the output of rn2().  I a lot of cases, all that the code
does is something like "if ( rn2( n ) =3D=3D 0 )", and you see is
whether the event happened or not.  Which looses a lot of
information.

